  "prefLabel": "Lab 103.01 Obtaining Records",
  "priorExpiration": "1998-03-16",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lab 103.01 Obtaining Records.\n\n(a) To the extent allowed by law, the records and reports of the department may be examined, and copied at their own expense, by any interested persons at the department offices, 95 Pleasant Street, Concord, New Hampshire 03301 from 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Monday through Friday on state workdays.\n\n(b) Copies of the records and reports may be obtained through a written request at a reasonable cost set by the department and which shall be paid by the requesting party.\n\n(c) All divisions of the department may be reached by telephone at (603) 271-3176.\n\nSource. #2264, eff 1-6-83; ss by #2935, eff 12-27-84, EXPIRED 12-27-90\n\nNew. #5235, eff 9-27-91, EXPIRED: 9-27-97\n\nNew. #6631, INTERIM, eff 11-16-97, EXPIRED: 3-16-98\n\nNew. #6805-A, eff 7-18-98",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lab100.html"
